(2863898, 395774, 58290, '<td valign="top">Ursula,<br/> <br/>Lovely lovely shot! Well done. I don''t want to see the original. I want to see what YOU see...always.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Ursula, Lovely lovely shot! Well done. I don''t want to see the original. I want to see what YOU see...always. ', '2006-09-25 17:21:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2863935, 397013, 43088, '<td valign="top">There is some nice color in the seeds. I would have tried to get closer to them.  I hope you like the D80 as much as I do! I found this picture by checking what other photos have been submitted with it. I have found that I need to be more careful about camera movement to avoid bluring since it shows more details.  I got the 18- 135mm kit lens with mine.</td>', 'There is some nice color in the seeds. I would have tried to get closer to them.  I hope you like the D80 as much as I do! I found this picture by checking what other photos have been submitted with it. I have found that I need to be more careful about camera movement to avoid bluring since it shows more details.  I got the 18- 135mm kit lens with mine.', '2006-09-25 17:33:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2863943, 396114, 43088, '<td valign="top">Sorry gang! I got my new camera and had a great shot that I wanted to do something with. You are right that it was not really on topic for this contest.</td>', 'Sorry gang! I got my new camera and had a great shot that I wanted to do something with. You are right that it was not really on topic for this contest.', '2006-09-25 17:36:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2864035, 395012, 18197, '<td valign="top">I neither entered nor voted the seed challenge. So I''m innocent! If I had voted, I might have given this a 4. <br/> <br/>Here is my "direct" reaction to the photo and the why behind the 4. I get the "life from death" motif but this doesn''t tell me or show me anything new in that respect. The seed pod has wonderful texture as does the sand with the terrific side lighting. I think if you had empahsized the textures and really focused on bringing them out, you photo would have scored higher. That probably requires a tighter crop, possibly the bottom and left 2/3rd of the frame. The sand just to the left of the pod is blown out so you have no chance with the texture there. Perhaps soften the lighting from the right and add a bit from the left to preserve all the texture available to you. The three little seeds detract IMO. They are just featureless black spots. Death from death in fact. If one of them was sprouted and some green was growing there would have been a purpose in having them there and your title would have worked splendidly. Or if there was a little rivulet (or even the equivelent of a dry stream bed, that might have implied the seeds could survive.</td>', 'I neither entered nor voted the seed challenge. So I''m innocent! If I had voted, I might have given this a 4.  Here is my "direct" reaction to the photo and the why behind the 4. I get the "life from death" motif but this doesn''t tell me or show me anything new in that respect. The seed pod has wonderful texture as does the sand with the terrific side lighting. I think if you had empahsized the textures and really focused on bringing them out, you photo would have scored higher. That probably requires a tighter crop, possibly the bottom and left 2/3rd of the frame. The sand just to the left of the pod is blown out so you have no chance with the texture there. Perhaps soften the lighting from the right and add a bit from the left to preserve all the texture available to you. The three little seeds detract IMO. They are just featureless black spots. Death from death in fact. If one of them was sprouted and some green was growing there would have been a purpose in having them there and your title would have worked splendidly. Or if there was a little rivulet (or even the equivelent of a dry stream bed, that might have implied the seeds could survive.', '2006-09-25 18:26:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2864041, 397407, 42826, '<td valign="top">what a great photo...love all the colors!!!</td>', 'what a great photo...love all the colors!!!', '2006-09-25 18:32:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2864090, 397324, 40952, '<td valign="top">I guess some people just didn''t get it. The concept for this shot was that a seed did survive (thus the title "Survivor") in this starkness. The seed grew in spite of the harshness of it''s surroundings into this tree. Some seeds will infact lay dormant for thousands of years until the conditions are right for it to sprout.<br/>Unfortunately, the shot was not viewed in this light. Such is life!</td>', 'I guess some people just didn''t get it. The concept for this shot was that a seed did survive (thus the title "Survivor") in this starkness. The seed grew in spite of the harshness of it''s surroundings into this tree. Some seeds will infact lay dormant for thousands of years until the conditions are right for it to sprout.Unfortunately, the shot was not viewed in this light. Such is life!', '2006-09-25 18:58:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2864109, 396924, 49497, '<td valign="top">Congrats!  Cute little critter!  MMM</td>', 'Congrats!  Cute little critter!  MMM', '2006-09-25 19:14:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2864112, 396655, 20168, '<td valign="top">Lovely photo Jason! Way to continue to put Oregon on the DPC map of the world! May your "seeds" continue to scatter and take root, bringing beauty and fruitfulness.</td>', 'Lovely photo Jason! Way to continue to put Oregon on the DPC map of the world! May your "seeds" continue to scatter and take root, bringing beauty and fruitfulness.', '2006-09-25 19:14:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2864115, 395012, 52449, '<td valign="top">The bokeh is nice, but there is a loss of detail in the right side of the mound (it''s a little washed out).<br/> <br/>Like the others, I didn''t get it. My first thoughts were a pecan (or even a dead leaf) with raisins. With "death" in the title, that''s what made me think of a dead leaf.<br/> <br/>What did you use for the sand effect? If it was brown sand (or you wanted a sepia effect), then the color cast is good. If it was salt, then there may be some color cast issues.<br/> <br/>I''ve entered dozens of photographs (mostly in other mediums, not DPC)and have come to face the fact that not everyone can be moved, and not everyone''s "hot buttons" pushed, by every photograph that you enter or display. There are always a great number of viewers that just won''t "get it" and DPC is no different.<br/> <br/>At any rate, keep up the good work (I''ve perused your portfolio) and you''ll get some great constructive feedback. "Patience, my young grasshopper."  :D<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-09-25 18:18:07.</i></td>', 'The bokeh is nice, but there is a loss of detail in the right side of the mound (it''s a little washed out). Like the others, I didn''t get it. My first thoughts were a pecan (or even a dead leaf) with raisins. With "death" in the title, that''s what made me think of a dead leaf. What did you use for the sand effect? If it was brown sand (or you wanted a sepia effect), then the color cast is good. If it was salt, then there may be some color cast issues. I''ve entered dozens of photographs (mostly in other mediums, not DPC)and have come to face the fact that not everyone can be moved, and not everyone''s "hot buttons" pushed, by every photograph that you enter or display. There are always a great number of viewers that just won''t "get it" and DPC is no different. At any rate, keep up the good work (I''ve perused your portfolio) and you''ll get some great constructive feedback. "Patience, my young grasshopper."  :D', '2006-09-25 19:16:26.000000', '2006-09-25 19:18:07.000000', 0),
